```verilog
module TopModule (
    input clk,
    input [7:0] in,
    output reg [7:0] anyedge
);

    reg [7:0] in_prev;

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        anyedge <= in ^ in_prev;
        in_prev <= in;
    end

endmodule
```

`in_prev` stores the previous clock cycle’s input value. On each positive clock edge, `anyedge` is set to `1` for any bit where the current input differs from the previous input.
